================================================================================

Seizure Memo Ref: {{NOTICE_ID}}
Case File Ref: {{CASE_ID}}
Date of Seizure: {{DATE}}
Place of Seizure: {{PLACE}}

TO (PERSON IN POSSESSION / BUSINESS ENTITY):
Entity Name: {{BUSINESS_NAME}}
Premises Address: {{BUSINESS_ADDRESS}}

SEIZURE ORDER UNDER SECTION 15 OF LEGAL METROLOGY ACT, 2009:
WHEREAS on {{INSPECTION_DATE}}, during an inspection of the premises situated at {{BUSINESS_ADDRESS}}, the undersigned Legal Metrology Officer has reason to believe that the pre-packaged commodities specified below are non-compliant and violate the statutory requirements of the Legal Metrology Act, 2009 and the Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011:

SCHEDULE OF SEIZED PACKAGES / COMMODITIES:
1. Commodity / Product Name: {{PRODUCT_NAME}}
2. Manufacturer / Packer / Importer: {{MANUFACTURER_NAME}}
3. Batch / Lot Number: {{BATCH_NUMBER}}
4. Declared MRP & Net Quantity: {{MRP}} | {{NET_QUANTITY}}
5. Nature of Contravention: {{OBSERVED_VIOLATION}}
6. Contravention of Statutory Law: {{LEGAL_SECTION}} read with {{LEGAL_RULE}}
7. Statutory Penal Provision: {{PENALTY}}
8. Response / Representation Deadline: {{DEADLINE}} days

CUSTODY DIRECTION UNDER RULE 20(1)(i) & RULE 20(2):
The aforesaid packages have been seized as material evidence under Section 15(1)(b) of the Act and Rule 20(1)(i) of the Rules. Representative sample packages have been drawn for production in Court or testing in accordance with Rule 19 and Rule 20(1). The disposal of seized packages shall be carried out in accordance with Section 15(3) of the Act and the provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (2 of 1974). You are strictly prohibited from removing, altering, selling, or tampering with any part of the seized stock under custody.

Seizing Authority:
Officer Name: {{INSPECTOR_NAME}}
Designation: {{OFFICER_AUTHORITY}}
Officer ID: {{INSPECTOR_ID}}
Signature & Official Seal: _______________________________

