- Contravention of Statutory Rule: {{LEGAL_RULE}} [Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011]
- Applicable Regular Penal Section: {{PENALTY}}

WHEREAS the applicant has submitted an application for compounding of the said offence under Section 48(1) of the Act;
AND WHEREAS the undersigned Compounding Authority has verified from records that this is a FIRST OFFENCE, and that no previous offence of similar nature has been compounded within the preceding three years under Section 48(2);

COMPOUNDING DETERMINATION UNDER RULE 32A:
Now, therefore, in exercise of powers conferred under Section 48(1) of the Legal Metrology Act, 2009 read with the Table under Rule 32A of the Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011, the undersigned Authority compounds the said offence upon payment of the statutory compounding fee specified below:

- Compounding Amount Payable: ₹{{COMPOUNDING_AMOUNT}}
- Treasury Payment Head: 0435 - Other Agricultural Programmes / Legal Metrology Receipts
- Payment Deadline: Within {{DEADLINE}} days from the date of this order

EFFECT OF COMPOUNDING:
Upon deposit of the aforesaid compounding amount and submission of proof of payment, no further prosecution proceedings shall be instituted against the offender in Court for the said offence, and any property seized in connection therewith shall be released in accordance with Section 48(3) of the Act.

